      "title": "Work Study",
      "description": "Missouri State University Applicant Portal | Work Study - Front Desk Worker (Downtown Campus) - Foreign Language Institute Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Missouri State University Office of Human Resources Part-Time Staff Positions Work Study - Front Desk Worker (Downtown Campus) - Foreign Language Institute Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Work Study - Front Desk Worker (Downtown Campus) - Foreign Language Institute Student Status Work Study Required- You are required to be a Federal Work Study Recipient to hold this position. Work Location Springfield Campus Department Languages, Cultures and Religions Hiring Range 15.00/hr Sponsorship Information Applicants must be currently authorized to work for ANY employer in the United States on a full-time basis. This position is not eligible for work visa sponsorship. Department/Employer Operating Hours MTWR 5:00 pm - 8:00pm How many hours per week are required? 8-12 Description of Primary Duties Arrive and leave on time for scheduled shifts. (All shifts are EVENING only.) Be attentive to monitor building traffic. Greet guests of the Jim D. Morris Center and the FLI . Answer questions pertaining to FLI classes. Communicate any building concerns with Safety and Transportation. Assist the FLI social media student worker with some tasks. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Excellent communication skills, the ability to be courteous and respectful when interacting with colleagues, students, supervisors, and others in the building and while on duty, and the ability to arrive and leave on time for scheduled shifts. Required Certifications Additional Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Contact Information fli@missouristate.edu Disclaimer Disclaimer for off campus positions only. #STU Equal Opportunity Statement Non-Discrimination Statement Missouri